"""Reviewed D2 task decisions; original reference docs and hosted builds stay distinct."""
P='/d2-survivors/'
THREAD='https://www.reddit.com/r/diablo2/comments/1x7g4ss/have_you_ever_wondered_what_would_diablo_2_look/'
DOC='https://d2survivors.lol/wiki/'
S={
 'start':(DOC+'getting-started/','D2 Survivors · Getting started','Original reference, checked 3 November 2026; menus can differ from the running build.'),
 'run':(DOC+'a-run/','D2 Survivors · A run','Original reference for acts and card choices, not a completed-run test.'),
 'save':(DOC+'saves/','D2 Survivors · Saves','Current original reference; not a promise of older hosted-version compatibility.'),
 'skills':(DOC+'skill-systems/','D2 Survivors · Skill systems','Original reference for resting skills and recharge.'),
 'stats':(DOC+'stats/','D2 Survivors · Stats','Original reference; the numbers below are not D2R breakpoints.'),
 'camp':(DOC+'camp/','D2 Survivors · The camp','Original reference for Akara and the waypoint; not all older builds show this camp.'),
 'werewolf':(DOC+'skills/druid/werewolf/','D2 Survivors · Werewolf','Original skill reference, not an independent build benchmark.'),
 'setup':('https://d2survivors.lol/play/setup.html','D2 Survivors · File setup','Original setup page inspected 3 November 2026; no personal game files selected.'),
 'download':('https://d2survivors.lol/download/','D2 Survivors · Desktop app','Original download instructions read in Chrome; installers not executed.'),
 'faq':('https://d2survivors.lol/faq/','D2 Survivors · FAQ','Original platform and language answers checked 3 November 2026.'),
 'thread':(THREAD,'Reddit · original-game discussion','Historical player questions; relative ages differ between cached views. Not a count of current bugs.'),
 'original':('https://d2survivors.lol/play/','D2 Survivors · Original game','Original menu and game-interface captures, 3 November 2026; displayed menu build 20261102.2. Short interface inspection only.'),
}

PAGES=[
dict(id='DS22',slug='beginners-guide',title='D2 Survivors Beginner Guide: Menus, Skills & Acts',h1='Start a run without following the wrong version',desc='Start D2 Survivors through the menu your version shows, choose skills and recognize act progression. Original and older hosted routes stay separate.',image='druid-card',alt='Druid starting skill choices in the original D2 Survivors game',caption='Original game interface, captured 3 November 2026 after choosing Druid. Initial card choices only; not a tested build or a complete act.',sources=['start','skills','run','thread','original'],answer='Match your host and menu first. A class-selection screen and the newer reference’s camp/waypoint flow need different steps. Choose an opening skill, move through the horde, then follow the act transition; entering a named area alone is not proof of reaching the next act.',sections=[
 ('start','Choose the route you can actually see','<p>For the original, open its own website and finish any file setup first. In the reference’s camp flow, choose a hero around the bonfire and use the waypoint to start. If your build instead shows Select Hero Class, choose a class and use its Start control. Our original-interface capture showed that class selector; the reference describes a later camp flow. Do not search an old menu indefinitely for a waypoint it does not show. {{start}}</p><p>The <a href="/d2-survivors/play/">hosted Play window</a> is another edition with separate progress. Follow its visible menu rather than assuming the original’s current documentation is a version match.</p>'),
 ('cards','Make a usable first choice','<p>Read the offered active skill and the passive separately. A new damaging skill gives you an attack to work around; a passive modifies your options but is not automatically a new attack. Keep your next picks consistent with the skill you chose. This is an opening decision method, not a ranked best-class claim. Slot limits, evolutions and requirements belong to the displayed build’s skill rules. {{skills}}</p><p>Use WASD to move and Esc to pause in the checked desktop route. Click inside the game if keys reach the webpage. Inventory and skill panels are references, not reasons to stand in a moving horde. {{start}}</p>'),
 ('acts','An area name is not another act','<p>The checked original reference advances areas on the act’s clock; walk across the incoming terrain border to enter the next area. Around six minutes of that act’s clock, its boss appears. Card and menu time pauses the clock, so six minutes on a wall clock is not the same test. The five act bosses are Andariel, Duriel, Mephisto, Diablo and Baal, in that order. A new area label is not a new act: finish the act boss sequence, then enter the red portal. The reference says to click the portal or stand still in it briefly; merely walking through it does not trigger the transfer. Pick up wanted equipment before leaving, because gear left on the floor stays in that act. A player explicitly asked how areas and acts differ; this is the distinction to check. These are dated reference rules, not a timed clear of the older hosted edition. {{run}}{{thread}}</p>'),
 ('next','Stop with a backup plan','<p>Before closing, use the save-and-exit control your build offers. If you want to resume, <a href="/d2-survivors/saves/">check Continue and the saved-run location</a> before choosing a fresh run. For a first installation, <a href="/d2-survivors/setup/">choose browser or desktop setup</a>. This guide does not certify boss clears or save transfers.</p>')]),
dict(id='DSX01',slug='setup',title='D2 Survivors Setup: Files, Desktop & Steam Deck',h1='Choose a file setup that matches your game host',desc='Choose the original D2 Survivors browser or desktop route, prepare Diablo II or D2R files, and read the documented Steam Deck path with version limits.',image='setup',alt='Original D2 Survivors setup offers Use my own files and a temporary Hosted Files route',caption='Original setup screen, inspected 3 November 2026. The Hosted Files option warns it is going away; no personal files were selected or extracted.',sources=['setup','download','start','faq'],answer='For the original, prepare your own Diablo II: Lord of Destruction 1.14 or Diablo II: Resurrected installation. Choose browser setup or the original desktop package; a third-party hosted game is a separate edition, not a way to prove the original needs no files.',sections=[
 ('choose','Browser, desktop or a hosted edition?','<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th>Route</th><th>Choose it for</th><th>Check first</th></tr><tr><td>Original browser</td><td>Playing in a desktop browser</td><td>Your own installation and available browser storage</td></tr><tr><td>Original desktop app</td><td>A separate app window and documented offline play after preparation</td><td>Original download and your operating system</td></tr><tr><td>Hosted Play window</td><td>Trying that provider’s older browser edition</td><td>Different version and separate progress</td></tr></table></div><p>Use <a href="https://d2survivors.lol/play/setup.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D2 Survivors · original setup ↗</a> or <a href="https://d2survivors.lol/download/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D2 Survivors · original downloads ↗</a>. We do not mirror installers or game archives. {{setup}}{{download}}</p>'),
 ('files','Prepare the right directory','<p>For classic LoD, the original reference lists d2data.mpq, d2char.mpq, d2sfx.mpq, d2exp.mpq and patch_d2.mpq; music and speech archives are optional. For D2R, select that installation or its containing library rather than trying to rename D2R files into classic MPQs. In browser setup, select the folder, follow EXTRACT and wait for completion. {{start}}</p><p>A temporary Hosted Files button is not a permanent file-free promise. Check the current message before selecting it. Do not delete saved browser data just because a newer build asks to read files again. {{setup}}</p>'),
 ('deck','The documented Steam Deck path','<p>The original download page lists a Linux x64 AppImage. Its instructions say to allow it to execute, open it in desktop mode and add it to Steam as a non-Steam game. If it cannot find the Diablo installation, the author points to its Wine/Proton prefix. This is the author’s app route, not the same procedure as an older browser/Flatseal tutorial. We have not installed it on a Deck. {{download}}</p>'),
 ('checks','Separate an error from a safety verdict','<p>Before retrying, record the exact host, app or browser version, chosen directory and error. A shortcut is not an installation directory. Check that the installation has finished updating, then follow the current setup message. A warning or an installer filename alone cannot certify safety; do not disable protection on the strength of this page. {{setup}}</p><p>Before switching app, browser or provider, <a href="/d2-survivors/saves/">export backups from both sides</a>. The original currently recommends a computer; old mobile setup advice has transition limits. {{faq}}</p>')]),
dict(id='DSX02',slug='saves',title='D2 Survivors Saves: Continue, Export & Host Checks',h1='Find Continue before starting another run',desc='Find a saved D2 Survivors run, distinguish Continue from New Run, and move Softcore progress with source and destination backups. Keep hosts separate.',image='saves',alt='Original D2 Survivors SAVES dialog with Export, Save as a file, and Import controls',caption='Original SAVES dialog, captured 3 November 2026 in a clean browser profile with no developed hero. It demonstrates the interface, not a successful progress migration.',sources=['save','camp','thread','original'],answer='Stay with the same host, browser profile, class and mode. Check the saved-run entry before selecting a new run. In the original’s camp reference, Continue is listed by the waypoint under the saved act; a new-run choice can replace it. Export backups before importing or changing hosts.',sections=[
 ('find','Imported a save but only see a new game?','<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th>Check</th><th>What to do before changing anything</th></tr><tr><td>Host and browser profile</td><td>Return to the exact place that created the save; another website does not automatically see it</td></tr><tr><td>Class and mode</td><td>Select the intended hero and Softcore/Hardcore save</td></tr><tr><td>Menu generation</td><td>Camp: inspect the waypoint’s saved act. Class-selector build: inspect that hero’s Continue option</td></tr><tr><td>New run warning</td><td>Read the replacement warning instead of clicking again to find Continue</td></tr></table></div><p>A player asked this after importing a save. It is a menu/host diagnosis, not proof that every missing Continue means the save is corrupt. {{thread}}{{save}}{{camp}}</p>'),
 ('backup','Export, back up the destination, then inspect','<ol><li>Save and exit on the source. Open SAVES and export a file or code; keep it privately.</li><li>If the destination already has progress, export that separately too.</li><li>Import only the intended source into the intended destination. Read its preview and replacement notice.</li><li>Check hero, equipment and the run entry before relying on the new location. Keep both backups.</li></ol><p>The current original permits Softcore export/import, not Hardcore migration. This is not a verified cross-version transfer procedure for the older hosted player. We do not upload or inspect your saves. {{save}}</p>'),
 ('continue','Continue is an act checkpoint','<p>The current original reference says Continue restarts the saved act at its start state, rather than restoring every second of movement. Other waypoint starts can end that saved run and ask for confirmation. Do not interpret an act restart alone as lost account progress. Older editions can retain different details, so follow their own warnings. {{save}}</p>'),
 ('tabs','A second tab and a different version are different problems','<p>The original can make a second tab wait while the first owns the save. Close the other game tab before treating the waiting screen as a failed import. If you changed providers, return to the old host rather than clearing storage. If loading fails repeatedly, preserve the backup and report the build and exact message; we cannot guarantee recovery. {{save}}</p><p><a href="/d2-survivors/setup/">Check the installation route →</a> · <a href="/d2-survivors/#versions">Identify the edition →</a></p>')]),
dict(id='DS23',slug='druid-skills',title='D2 Survivors Druid: Rest Skills or Re-draft?',h1='Rest an unwanted skill or rebuild the Druid?',desc='Separate resting a D2 Survivors Druid skill from re-drafting at Akara. Match old shapeshift reports to current rules and protect the saved run first.',image='skill-tree',alt='Original D2 Survivors Druid skill tree showing Elemental and Shape Shifting tabs',caption='Original Druid interface capture, 3 November 2026. Skill-tree inspection is not a test of shapeshift recovery, respec or a ranked build.',sources=['skills','camp','werewolf','thread','original'],answer='Resting stops a skill from casting while retaining its slot; it is not a respec. For a rebuild, the current original reference describes Akara’s Re-draft after that hero’s first Baal kill. Neither is a verified instant fix for every historical shapeshift report.',sections=[
 ('rest','First decide what you want to change','<p>Want to stop an unwanted cast? The current original reference says to right-click the skill slot during a run to rest it, and repeat to enable it again. The slot and learned level remain. Want to choose a different set of skills? That requires a re-draft route rather than resting every skill. {{skills}}</p><p>Old community replies suggested resting Werewolf/Werebear when an elemental Druid was disrupted. Those are historical reports; preventing another cast and ending a transformation already active are different claims. We have not reproduced that bug or certified a universal fix. {{thread}}{{werewolf}}</p>'),
 ('redraft','Check Akara’s condition before planning a reset','<p>The current camp reference locks Re-draft and Start over until the hero’s first Baal kill. Read the option you are confirming: re-drafting skills and returning to level 1 are distinct choices, with confirmation steps. Back up first, and inspect any saved-run warning. These instructions describe the reference’s camp version; do not search an older class-selector release for a feature it lacks. {{camp}}</p>'),
 ('report','If the expected skill still will not cast','<p>Record your host and displayed build, learned skills, active form and whether the skill is rested. Then check the skill’s actual targeting and form rules in that version. Avoid resetting the character just to test whether a button is hidden. <a href="/d2-survivors/saves/">Preserve the save</a> before reporting the symptom. This task guide does not rank the best Druid build or promise that all elemental skills behave alike.</p>')]),
dict(id='DS24',slug='attack-speed',title='D2 Survivors Attack Speed vs Faster Cast Rate',h1='Compare speed upgrades using Survivors rules',desc='Understand how Increased Attack Speed contributes to Faster Cast Rate in D2 Survivors, why D2R breakpoints do not apply, and how to compare two items.',image='character',alt='Original D2 Survivors character panel showing attributes and equipment',caption='Original character/equipment interface, captured 3 November 2026. The panel is context for comparing displayed stats, not a timed damage test.',sources=['stats','skills','thread','original'],answer='In the checked original reference, each point of item Increased Attack Speed adds half a point of Faster Cast Rate. Attacks and skills share the resulting speed system, and there are no D2R-style breakpoints. Compare the displayed total and the affected skill instead of copying a Diablo II gear threshold.',sections=[
 ('compare','Turn the item lines into a comparison','<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0"><table><tr><th>Hypothetical item line</th><th>Contribution under the checked reference</th></tr><tr><td>+20 Increased Attack Speed</td><td>+10 Faster Cast Rate before other modifiers and the curve</td></tr><tr><td>+20 Faster Cast Rate</td><td>+20 to that total before the curve</td></tr><tr><td>Both together</td><td>Add their contributions; do not treat them as two independent multipliers</td></tr></table></div><p>This example assumes the item line has its full applicable weight. For dual-wielded weapons, the reference weights each weapon’s IAS at half before that conversion; a +20 IAS line on one of those weapons therefore contributes +5 FCR, not +10. It is not a named-item recommendation or a promise that 20 more points means 20% more final DPS. The original character screen’s item preview is the useful next check. {{stats}}</p>'),
 ('limits','Raw speed is not final recharge reduction','<p>The reference applies diminishing returns and class-dependent caps. It explicitly says there are no breakpoints, so a D2R breakpoint table answers a different game’s question. Compare two items with your current class and skill present, keeping damage and defenses in the decision too. {{stats}}</p><p>A skill also needs a valid target before it casts. Item skill modifiers and innate hastes can affect recharge; an idle or rested skill is not evidence that a speed item failed. {{skills}}</p>'),
 ('check','Use the same host and a controlled comparison','<ol><li>Note the game host and build, class, skill and current equipment.</li><li>Read the displayed total before and after the one item change.</li><li>Keep the skill, target situation and other equipment fixed if you compare actual cast behavior.</li><li>If your display disagrees, keep the screenshot and exact item lines; do not transplant a newer formula into an old hosted edition.</li></ol><p>Players asked whether familiar Diablo II speed rules carried over. This guide separates that question from damage-per-second rankings. We have not timed a benchmark or established the current best item. {{thread}}</p>')]),
dict(id='DS03',slug='ko',lang='ko',title='D2 서바이버 가이드: 원본, 설치와 저장',h1='디아2 뱀서: 원본과 플레이 경로부터 고르세요',desc='D2 Survivors 원본과 이전 호스팅 버전을 구분하고, 설치 파일·시작 메뉴·저장 데이터 확인 순서로 안내합니다. 비공식 가이드입니다.',image='original-menu',alt='D2 Survivors 원본의 PLAY, OPTIONS, SAVES 메뉴',caption='2026년 11월 3일 원본 메뉴 캡처. 표시된 빌드 20261102.2, 화면은 영어입니다. 한국어 패치 설치나 저장 이전 테스트가 아닙니다.',sources=['faq','start','save','original'],answer='D2 Survivors는 디아블로 II를 바탕으로 한 비공식 서바이버 게임입니다. 원본을 시작할지, 이 사이트의 이전 호스팅 버전을 시작할지 먼저 고르세요. 서로 다른 사이트의 저장 데이터는 자동으로 이어지지 않습니다.',sections=[
 ('choose','원본과 호스팅 버전은 다릅니다','<p>원본 주소는 d2survivors.lol입니다. 원본 FAQ는 자신의 디아블로 II와 파괴의 군주 1.14 또는 레저렉션 설치 파일이 필요하다고 설명합니다. 공식 사이트와 게임은 영어 및 한국어를 안내하지만, 별도 팬 번역 도구는 다른 제작자의 프로젝트입니다. {{faq}}</p><p><a href="https://d2survivors.lol/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D2 Survivors · 원본 ↗</a> · <a href="/d2-survivors/play/">이 사이트의 게임 창 →</a>. 게임 창은 이전 타사 버전이며 원본 최신판으로 소개하지 않습니다.</p>'),
 ('start','보이는 메뉴에 맞게 시작하기','<p>야영지 버전은 웨이포인트에서 시작하고, 직업 선택 화면 버전은 영웅을 고른 뒤 Start를 사용합니다. 다른 버전의 설명을 보고 없는 버튼을 찾지 마세요. 이동하며 업그레이드를 선택하는 것이 기본 흐름이고, 기술은 자동으로 사용됩니다. {{start}}</p><p><a href="/d2-survivors/beginners-guide/">영어 시작 가이드 →</a> · <a href="/d2-survivors/setup/">설치 파일과 데스크톱 경로 →</a></p>'),
 ('save','새 판을 누르기 전에 저장 확인','<p>원래 사이트와 브라우저 프로필, 직업, 모드를 확인하세요. 저장된 진행이 있으면 Continue 항목을 먼저 찾고, 새 판 시작이나 가져오기의 교체 경고를 읽으세요. 원본은 Softcore 내보내기와 가져오기를 제공하지만 Hardcore 이전은 지원하지 않습니다. 이전 버전과의 호환성은 여기서 확인하지 않았습니다. {{save}}</p><p><a href="/d2-survivors/saves/">영어 저장·Continue 확인 순서 →</a>. 실제 휴대폰, 데스크톱 설치와 진행 복구 테스트는 하지 않았습니다.</p>')]),
]

def render(p,shell,figure,ext):
 import re
 sources=p['sources'];ko=p.get('lang')=='ko'
 def refs(text):return re.sub(r'\{\{(\w+)\}\}',lambda m:f'<sup class="ref"><a href="#source-{sources.index(m[1])+1}">[{sources.index(m[1])+1}]</a></sup>',text)
 toc='<aside class="toc"><strong>'+('목차'if ko else'On this page')+'</strong>'+''.join(f'<a href="#{i}">{t}</a>'for i,t,_ in p['sections'])+'</aside>'
 body=f'<nav class="crumbs"><a href="{P}">D2 Survivors</a> / {p["h1"]}</nav><header class="article-head" id="guide"><span class="tag">Independent game guide</span><h1>{p["h1"]}</h1><div class="answer"><p>{p["answer"]}</p></div><p class="meta">Megabonk.org editors · Checked 3 November 2026 · Original references and dated interface captures; no complete-run or save-migration test.</p></header><div class="article-layout">{toc}<article class="prose">'
 for n,(i,t,c)in enumerate(p['sections']):
  body+=f'<section id="{i}"><h2>{t}</h2>{refs(c)}</section>'
  if n==0:body+=figure(p['image'],p['alt'],p['caption']+' Game art © Blizzard Entertainment / respective owners.',sources.index('original')+1 if 'original'in sources else 1)
 body+='<section class="sources" id="sources"><h2>'+('출처와 확인 범위'if ko else'Sources & limits')+'</h2><p>Original reference pages share one publisher. A current reference and an older playable build can differ; no cross-version compatibility or universal fix is claimed.</p><ol>'+''.join(f'<li id="source-{n}">{ext(S[k][0],S[k][1])} — {S[k][2]}</li>'for n,k in enumerate(sources,1))+'</ol><a href="#guide">'+('본문으로 ↑'if ko else'Back to guide ↑')+'</a></section><section class="related"><h2>'+('다음 단계'if ko else'Choose your next task')+'</h2><p><a href="'+P+'#guides">All D2 Survivors guides →</a></p>'+''.join(f'<p><a href="{P+q["slug"]}/">{q["title"]} →</a></p>'for q in PAGES if q['slug']in ['beginners-guide','setup','saves']and q['slug']!=p['slug'])+'</section></article></div>'
 return shell(P+p['slug']+'/',p['title'],p['desc'],body,p.get('lang','en')).replace('https://megabonk.org/assets/d2-survivors/original-menu-1280.webp','https://megabonk.org/assets/d2-survivors/'+p['image']+'-1280.webp')
